# Copy to `.env` or `.env.local` for local dev. Never commit real secrets.

# Postgres — Supabase (https://supabase.com) or Neon (https://console.neon.tech).
# Encode reserved URI characters in the password (e.g. `@` → `%40`, `#` → `%23`).
#
# --- Supabase + Prisma (default in this repo: pooler + directUrl) ---
# Direct host `db.<ref>.supabase.co` is often IPv6-only; Windows/dev may get P1001 "Can't reach database".
# Use Supabase → Settings → Database → Connection pooling (IPv4 pooler):
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&sslmode=require"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require"
#
# Neon or any Postgres with IPv4: you can use a single DATABASE_URL and remove `directUrl` from prisma/schema.prisma.
#
# Optional: only if you use @supabase/supabase-js in the browser
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
#
# Vercel: set DATABASE_URL and DIRECT_URL (both required with this repo’s schema). No extra wrapping quotes in the UI.
#
# --- Supabase / fresh Postgres ---
# `prisma/migrations/` only contains *incremental* changes; it assumes a `User` table (Auth.js baseline) already existed
# when migrations were authored. On a brand-new empty Supabase DB, run ONE of:
#   A) npx prisma db push          — creates/updates all tables to match schema.prisma (simplest for new DBs)
#   B) npx prisma migrate deploy   — only if you restored from Neon (or otherwise have matching baseline + _prisma_migrations)
# Verify against Prisma (empty script output = DB matches schema.prisma):
#   npm run db:drift-check
# Quick check that DATABASE_URL credentials work (fails with P1000 until password/user are correct).
# Uses the same .env + .env.local merge and quote-stripping as the Next.js app:
#   npm run db:ping
# If OAuth shows error=Configuration and the dev terminal logs "column … does not exist" (e.g. User.accountDeletedAt),
# your DB is behind prisma/schema.prisma — run: npx prisma db push   (or migrate deploy on a baselined DB).
# Or paste scripts/supabase-schema-audit.sql into Supabase SQL Editor.
# Prisma + Supabase: https://www.prisma.io/docs/orm/overview/databases/supabase

# --- Prisma migrations (production) ---
# This repo keeps history in `prisma/migrations/`. Prefer `prisma migrate deploy` (not `db push`) so the
# DB matches those migrations exactly. Do NOT rely on `migrate deploy` inside Vercel "npm run build" if
# the pooler times out (P1002): run `npm run migrate:deploy` after deploy from CI or your machine.

# Optional: Upstash Redis — https://upstash.com (Vercel Marketplace). Speeds up repeated API reads (dashboard, chat list, slots).
# If omitted, the app runs unchanged without Redis.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Auth.js / NextAuth — `npx auth secret` for AUTH_SECRET in production.
# Required on Vercel (build fails if missing). Local `next dev` uses a dev-only fallback when unset — still set AUTH_SECRET for stable sessions across restarts.
#
# This codebase does NOT use Better Auth — `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` is ignored. Use AUTH_SECRET only.

AUTH_SECRET=
# NEXTAUTH_SECRET=

# Canonical site URL (no trailing slash). Must match the URL in the browser (https, www vs non-www).
# Local dev — use this in `.env` / `.env.local`:
AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Strongly recommended: set NEXTAUTH_URL to the SAME value as AUTH_URL (Auth.js client reads NEXTAUTH_URL first).
# If you only set AUTH_URL, `next.config.ts` copies it to NEXTAUTH_URL at build time — but setting both explicitly is clearest.
# NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Production — set in Vercel/hosting env only (pick ONE canonical host — apex or www — and stick to it):
# AUTH_URL=https://commonsia.com
# NEXTAUTH_URL=https://commonsia.com
# Or:
# AUTH_URL=https://www.commonsia.com
# NEXTAUTH_URL=https://www.commonsia.com

# --- Sign-in checklist (local) ---
# 1) AUTH_SECRET — `npx auth secret` → paste into .env (required on Vercel; recommended locally).
# 2) AUTH_URL — exact browser origin, e.g. http://localhost:3000 (no trailing slash).
# 3) DATABASE_URL + DIRECT_URL — Supabase: use pooler URLs from the dashboard (see above); direct db.* host often fails on Windows.
# 4) Tables — new DB: `npx prisma db push` OR (if you have Neon history) `npx prisma migrate deploy`.
# 5) Restart `npm run dev`. Optional: `AUTH_DEBUG=1` then watch the terminal.
#
# --- Sign-in troubleshooting (students / OAuth) ---
# - AUTH_SECRET + AUTH_URL (and ideally NEXTAUTH_URL) must be set in production.
# - DATABASE_URL must be valid (Prisma adapter); failed DB → sign-in errors.
# - Google: use Web application OAuth client; redirect URI exactly `{AUTH_URL}/api/auth/callback/google`.
#   Main sign-in uses scopes `openid email profile` only. Calendar for mentors uses `/api/calendar/google/authorize` (separate consent).
# - LinkedIn: enable product "Sign in with LinkedIn using OpenID Connect"; redirect `{AUTH_URL}/api/auth/callback/linkedin`.
# - Browser URL must match AUTH_URL (e.g. don’t mix apex vs www, or http vs https).

# Google — sign-in vs Calendar/Meet (recommended: two OAuth clients in Cloud Console).
#
# Sign-in (`/api/auth/callback/google`): use GOOGLE_LOGIN_* (or legacy GOOGLE_CLIENT_* / AUTH_GOOGLE_*).
GOOGLE_LOGIN_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_LOGIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Legacy aliases still supported:
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=
#
# Calendar connect (`/api/calendar/google/*`) + GOOGLE_ADMIN_REFRESH_TOKEN must use the **same**
# OAuth client that minted the refresh token. Prefer a dedicated client:
GOOGLE_MEET_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_MEET_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# Workspace calendar used when neither student nor mentor can host the event (admin fallback).
# Refresh token from OAuth consent on an account that can create Meet links for org policy.
GOOGLE_ADMIN_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# Optional: calendar ID for admin inserts (`primary` default). Use the organizer mailbox if not primary.
ADMIN_EMAIL=hello@commonsia.com

LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID=
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Fallback: AUTH_LINKEDIN_ID, AUTH_LINKEDIN_SECRET
# LinkedIn app → Products: enable "Sign in with LinkedIn using OpenID Connect"

# --- OAuth consoles: redirect URIs must match AUTH_URL exactly (https, www, path) ---
#
# Google Cloud → APIs & Services → Credentials → your Web client → Authorized redirect URIs.
# Register EVERY URI you use. **Sign-in client** vs **Meet/Calendar client** may differ; both need:
#   {AUTH_URL}/api/auth/callback/google
#   {AUTH_URL}/api/calendar/google/callback
#
# Local dev: if you open the site as http://127.0.0.1:3000, add those too (Calendar OAuth
# uses the browser host so it matches). Example extras:
#   http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/auth/callback/google
#   http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/calendar/google/callback
#
# LinkedIn Developers → your app → Auth → Redirect URLs:
#   {AUTH_URL}/api/auth/callback/linkedin
#
# If you see "Error 400: redirect_uri_mismatch", add the exact redirect_uri from the error
# (or the two URIs above for BOTH localhost and 127.0.0.1 if you use either).
#
# Production debugging (Vercel): set AUTH_DEBUG=1 temporarily, redeploy, check logs, then remove.
# Ensure `prisma migrate deploy` runs (included in `npm run build` for Vercel).

# Optional: IANA timezone passed to Google Calendar event start/end (default Asia/Kolkata).
# DEFAULT_CALENDAR_TIMEZONE=Asia/Kolkata

# Optional: Resend (https://resend.com) — sends a confirmation email to student + mentor when a session is booked.
# Without this, only Google Calendar guest invites apply (organizer may not get a separate email from Google).
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# Use ONE verified domain sender for both recipients (not the student’s personal Gmail), e.g.:
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=Commonsia <bookings@yourdomain.com>
# Google Calendar may still send invites from Google’s mail servers when the event lives on Calendar; Resend is independent.

# --- Booking requests (mentor approval via WhatsApp + webhook) ---
#
# === After a session is booked (accepted / slot confirmed) ===
# Commonsia notifies student + mentor via Zixflow using WhatsApp digits from profile `whatsappUrl`,
# then `phone` if WhatsApp is empty. Configure BOTH templates for production:
#   ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_CONFIRMED_TEMPLATE — message to the student
#   ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_CONFIRMED_MENTOR_TEMPLATE — message to the mentor
# Successful sends set `MentoringBooking.whatsappStudentNotifiedAt` / `whatsappMentorNotifiedAt`
# (requires migration `20260501140000_mentoring_booking_whatsapp_audit`). Apply with:
#   npx prisma migrate deploy
#
# Zixflow WhatsApp — https://docs.zixflow.com/api-reference/campaign/whatsapp/send-whatsapp-message.md
# Optional — defaults to https://api.zixflow.com when unset ([API docs](https://docs.zixflow.com/api-reference/introduction)).
# ZIXFLOW_BASE_URL=https://api.zixflow.com
# ZIXFLOW_API_KEY=...
#
# Phone ID from Zixflow → Campaign → WhatsApp Settings (shown next to your WhatsApp number). Required to send.
# Example: +91 97598 44508 → Phone ID 1088160251051042
# ZIXFLOW_WHATSAPP_PHONE_ID=1088160251051042
#
# Template language code as registered in Zixflow (often "en" or "en_US").
# ZIXFLOW_WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_LANGUAGE=en
#
# If mentors save a 10-digit local number without country code, prepend this (e.g. India → 91).
# ZIXFLOW_DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE=91
#
# Dev/testing only: when the mentor profile has no WhatsApp URL, send booking-request templates here instead.
# Use digits only, no + (e.g. 919759844508 for +91 97598 44508).
# ZIXFLOW_FALLBACK_TO_DIGITS=
#
# Registered Meta/Zixflow template: **mentorship_session_booking** (“Mentorship Session Booking”).
# Example copy: Hello {{1}}, … {{2}} a {{3}} year student from {{4}} … Student Profile {{5}}, Requested Time {{6}}.
# Body mapping (default `ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_BODY_VARS_ORDER`): {{1}} mentor name, {{2}} student name,
# {{3}} year of study, {{4}} college, {{5}} student profile URL, {{6}} the session time that will be booked:
# the first mentor session-length slice at the start of the band the student picked (e.g. 10–12 PM band, 30 min → {{6}} is 10:00–10:30). Mentor “Yes”/Accept confirms that slice in DB + Calendar (unless catalog mode is on).
# Optional catalog flow (second WhatsApp step): set BOTH `ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_TIME_SLOTS_TEMPLATE` AND
# `BOOKING_SLOT_CATALOG_BEFORE_CONFIRM=true`. Otherwise Accept creates Calendar + Meet immediately.
# Configure Accept/Reject as Meta URL buttons mapped to Zixflow vars `acceptUrl` / `rejectUrl` → `/api/webhooks/zixflow?token=…` (signed).
# Do not point buttons at `/api/booking/accept?bookingId=…` — those URLs are rejected by design.
# Only extend ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_BODY_VARS_ORDER with acceptUrl etc. if your template defines extra body vars.
# ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_REQUEST_TEMPLATE=mentorship_session_booking
#
# Logical keys → body_1 … body_6 (match Zixflow “Get Template Variables”). Default:
# ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_BODY_VARS_ORDER=mentorName,studentName,year,college,studentProfile,requestedTime
#
# Second-step catalog template (optional). Meta {{1}}–{{4}} map to mentor/student/date/range + catalog URL body var.
# ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_TIME_SLOTS_TEMPLATE=time_slots
#
# Set true **only** with the template above so Accept sends catalog before Calendar + Meet.
# BOOKING_SLOT_CATALOG_BEFORE_CONFIRM=false
#
# Minutes between offered start times inside the student’s requested window (default 15).
# BOOKING_SLOT_CATALOG_STEP_MINUTES=15
#
# Five-variable default (catalog URL as body_5). Override with four keys only if your Meta template has no fifth body slot:
# ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_TIME_SLOTS_BODY_VARS_ORDER=mentorName,studentName,requestedDate,requestedRange,catalogUrl
#
# Optional: comma-separated logical keys → body_N for confirmation templates (student + mentor).
# Default when unset: studentName,mentorName,startISO,meetLink (override if your Meta template order differs).
# ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_CONFIRMED_BODY_VARS_ORDER=studentName,mentorName,startISO,meetLink
# ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_CONFIRMED_TEMPLATE=...
# ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_CONFIRMED_MENTOR_TEMPLATE=...
# ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_REJECTED_TEMPLATE=...
#
# Webhook URL for Zixflow must hit this host + `/api/webhooks/zixflow` — localhost does NOT work unless you tunnel.
# BOOKING_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://YOUR-NGROK.ngrok-free.app
# When set, Accept/Reject/catalog/student-profile links in WhatsApp use this origin instead of AUTH_URL (keep AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000 for OAuth).
#
# Optional: Zixflow variable **keyName** for Meta URL (CTA) buttons so Accept / Decline / catalog open without copy-paste.
# ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_ACCEPT_URL_TEMPLATE_VAR=
# ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_REJECT_URL_TEMPLATE_VAR=
# ZIXFLOW_BOOKING_CATALOG_URL_TEMPLATE_VAR=
#
# Token used to secure Accept/Reject links embedded in WhatsApp templates.
# BOOKING_ACTION_SECRET=change-me-long-random
#
# Dev: when true, POST /api/booking-requests includes `whatsapp` in JSON (skip reason or Zixflow error text — no secrets).
# BOOKING_WHATSAPP_DIAGNOSTICS=true
#
# CLI: `npm run booking:whatsapp-check` — verifies critical env keys are set (does not send WhatsApp).
